The advance is `nextCheck += threshold` - it is never rebased on `acc.Len()`. Since `acc.Len()` grows by the size of each text delta (`acc.WriteString(chunk.TextDelta)` at gateway.go:695) and a single SSE line may legally carry up to 4 MiB (gateway.go:640 `scanner.Buffer(make([]byte, 64<<10), 4<<20)`), any upstream whose deltas exceed `threshold` leaves `acc.Len() - nextCheck` permanently positive: from that crossing onward the condition at 699 is true on *every* subsequent text delta, so the whole-prefix scan (gateway.go:777 -> engine.go:136-153) runs once per token instead of once per `threshold` bytes - byte-work K*L*N (N = number of text deltas) rather than K*L^2/(2*threshold). The same drift cuts the other way for detection: after one large line, `nextCheck` sits thousands of bytes behind `acc.Len()`, so the per-threshold cadence in REQ-011 is not what the code delivers. The end-of-stream re-scan at gateway.go:749-750 also repeats a full scan of text already covered by the last crossing.

